  "solution": "For the quadratic \\(3x^2+4x-9\\), let the roots be \\(r\\) and \\(s\\).\n\nBy Vieta’s formulas:\n\n\\[\nr+s=-\\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nrs=\\frac{-9}{3}=-3\n\\]\n\nWe want \\(r^2+s^2\\). Using\n\n\\[\nr^2+s^2=(r+s)^2-2rs\n\\]\n\nwe get\n\n\\[\nr^2+s^2=\\left(-\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^2-2(-3)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n=\\frac{16}{9}+6\n\\]\n\n\\[\n=\\frac{16}{9}+\\frac{54}{9}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n=\\frac{70}{9}\n\\]\n\nThe answer is \\(\\frac{70}{9}\\).",
